  4905	- **Council** (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ml-codex-7.md` to `ml-codex-9.md`): resuming in place needed a recovery proof (`resume_check.py` could not fake a valid judgement for views opened on the stopped day); three fresh draws avoid it. Jev now settles its whole charge at three times its reported input tokens (a hidden retry is the same request), uncapped so that an excess sets the overrun flag; zero, missing or invalid usage settles at the whole reservation; the retry check goes through the real `jev.transport` with a fake network failure (`check_budget.py` 12 of 12; mutants caught). Consensus: "Council position: consensus on three fresh draws as in ml-challenge-7.md and ml-challenge-8.md".
  4906	- **Decided:** three fresh 14-day draws from empty (`draw-q1..q3`), the same day; a new shared ledger with ceiling $3.00, conditional on the reservation and retry-billing bounds (an overrun stops later sends but cannot undo a charge); run caps $1.00. The stopped p1–p3 are kept as records, unused; their recorded cost ($0.98) and ledger charge ($4.999) are reported separately. This replaces D443's $5 shared limit for these draws.
