codex
V3 addresses most round-five points. It separates release status from the verdict, preserves D400’s accounting minima, restores the search audit, uses the shipped renderer, and specifies D442’s July 14 outcome rules. I agree that an unmeasured hard check leaves release uncleared. Step 2 line 2 is buildable from `repeat_of` with the frozen third-reader rule. [V3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/DESIGN-1.6.md:20) · [Frozen rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/verdict-rule.json:77)

- **Step 2 line 1.** Treat whole-history scan hits as candidates. Put them through the same full-context labelling and adjudication before they enter the 100-record denominator. The original scan showed summaries and collected possible matches. [V3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/DESIGN-1.6.md:68) · [Original packet builder](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step2-validation-2026-11-07/build_reader_packets.py:40)
- **Step 2 line 3.** Keep the shipped renderer and paired totals. Give each rendering to a separate closed session within each family, with the surrounding dossier held fixed. V3 has each reader see both versions of a group. The recorded test used one view per reader, so a detail seen in one version could not carry into the other mark. [V3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/DESIGN-1.6.md:86) · [Recorded test](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step2-validation-2026-11-07/LOG.md:214)
- **D442 is buildable from the stores.** Its first-created match, D430 eligibility and outcome order carry over without the adapter. Enumerate every view created by July 14, including closed views, then read its `state_as_of`. The state reader retrieves judgements for a supplied view. It does not select the July library. [D442 procedure](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/DESIGN.md:43) · [Store readers](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:129)
- **Finish the diagnostic wiring.** V3 promises reports on finished draws after a stop, but eligibility exits on the first incomplete draw. Record fingerprints for finished draws before withholding the aggregate verdict. Label D428’s figures as guardrail-sample comparisons and report insufficient latest answers alongside them. [V3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/DESIGN-1.6.md:143) · [Eligibility](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/eligibility.py:89) · [D428](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4761)

CHANGE: adjudicate scan hits, isolate the paired dossier readings, make July view selection explicit, and preserve diagnostics for finished draws.
